"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[7002],{87002:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"slug":"aramco-skidka-aziya-g7-rezervy-neft","locale":"en","title":"Saudi Arabia’s largest Asian discount in 6 years makes it harder for Russia to sell oil above market prices","description":"Aramco gave Asia a $5-per-barrel discount, its largest since 2020, while G7 countries will release 100 million barrels from reserves. What this means for Russian oil and the ruble.","blocks":[{"id":"b001","kind":"paragraph","text":"Saudi Aramco set its flagship Arab Light crude price for Asian buyers in November 2026 at $5 per barrel below the local benchmark. October\'s discount was $2. It is the largest discount since June 2020, although traders and refiners had expected a price increase. This does not make Saudi oil cheap: the discount is measured against a traded benchmark, while Brent remains above $100. For Europe, Aramco instead raised its November price by $3, without explaining why."},{"id":"b002","kind":"paragraph","text":"This is how official selling prices work. Aramco sells most oil through long-term contracts and announces each month how much above or below a benchmark its barrels will cost. Like a wholesaler\'s price list, the product is unchanged, but the discount determines where the buyer goes. Two factors explain the cut for Asia. More oil is moving through the Strait of Hormuz again, and JPMorgan estimates Middle Eastern exports have recovered to roughly 98% of pre-war levels. Shipping has also become more expensive: hiring a large tanker from the Persian Gulf to China costs around $1.2 million daily, versus $80 thousand a year earlier. The discount partly offsets that cost for buyers."},{"id":"b003","kind":"paragraph","text":"Meanwhile, G7 countries agreed on October 2 to release 100 million barrels of oil and diesel from strategic reserves. Most diesel will be released in the first 20 days, with the rest over 4 months. On the morning of October 5, Brent was around $101.6 per barrel, down 0.65% from Friday. It remained above $100."},{"id":"b004","kind":"paragraph","text":"For Russia, the Asian part matters most. In September 2026, Russian Urals sold in China at roughly $15 per barrel above world prices and in India at $3.7 above them. Such a markup is called a premium; it was almost absent in August. These premiums include delivery to the buyer\'s port, and transport has become much more expensive. They rose when Persian Gulf oil was scarce and Indian and Chinese refiners sought substitutes. Gulf supply is now returning, while a major competitor is cutting prices for the same buyers, making those premiums harder to retain. October prices will reveal how far they fell. September\'s average Urals price used for mineral extraction tax was $92.08 per barrel, compared with $67.11 in August. This price determines oil companies\' budget payments."},{"id":"b005","kind":"paragraph","text":"For an ordinary person, this is not primarily a petrol story. Russian pump prices are supported by fuel-export restrictions and depend more on domestic refinery operations. The channel is different: lower oil revenue means less budget tax income and less foreign currency supplied to the market, putting pressure on the ruble. Buying currency because of one Saudi discount means betting on a chain of effects that has not yet materialised. Nor should September prices be treated as permanent protection for the ruble: whether Aramco keeps the discount in December and whether Hormuz stays open remain unknown."},{"id":"b006","kind":"heading","text":"Why did Saudi Arabia reduce its oil price for Asia?"},{"id":"b007","kind":"paragraph","text":"More oil is moving through Hormuz again, so producers must compete for buyers. Shipping costs have also risen: a large tanker to China costs around $1.2 million daily, and the discount partly compensates buyers. For Europe, Aramco instead raised November prices by $3."},{"id":"b008","kind":"heading","text":"How much oil will G7 countries release from reserves?"},{"id":"b009","kind":"paragraph","text":"100 million barrels of oil and diesel. Most diesel will be released in the first 20 days, and the remainder over 4 months."},{"id":"b010","kind":"heading","text":"How does the Saudi discount affect Russia?"},{"id":"b011","kind":"paragraph","text":"Through the price of Russian oil in Asia. In September, Urals sold roughly $15 above world prices in China and $3.7 above in India because Persian Gulf supply was scarce. Gulf volumes are now returning and Saudi oil is becoming cheaper for Asia, making these premiums harder to maintain. Lower revenue means less tax income and foreign currency."}],"sources":[{"label":"Saudi Arabia unexpectedly cuts November oil prices to Asia to 6-year lows","url":"https://gulfbusiness.com/en/2026/saudi-arabia/saudi-aramco-cuts-asia-oil-prices-six-year-low/"},{"label":"Saudis Cut Flagship Oil Price to Asia to Lowest in Six Years","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/energy/articles/saudis-cut-flagship-oil-price-010940614.html"},{"label":"Oil slips as Middle East crude exports rise, G7 to release stocks","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/energy/articles/oil-slips-middle-east-crude-013514252.html"},{"label":"G7 nations will release 100 million barrels of oil and diesel fuel after prices soar","url":"https://www.bnnbloomberg.ca/markets/oil/2026/10/02/g7-nations-agree-to-release-100-million-barrels-of-oil-including-diesel-a-boost-for-trump/"},{"label":"Urals rose in September in the Baltic, India and China as ESPO discounts became premiums","url":"https://www.interfax.ru/business/1119753"},{"label":"Urals premiums at Indian ports surged amid a shortage of Middle Eastern crude","url":"https://ru.themoscowtimes.com/2026/09/15/premii-na-neft-urals-vzleteli-v-portakh-indii-iz-za-defitsita-predlozheniya-blizhnevostochnogo-syrya-treydery-a206168"},{"label":"Average Urals crude prices for August 2026","url":"https://www.garant.ru/hotlaw/federal/2228866/"},{"label":"Russian government extends the diesel-export ban to all market participants","url":"https://neftegaz.ru/news/gosreg/937606-pravitelstvo-rf-prodlilo-zapret-na-eksport-diztopliva-dlya-vsekh-uchastnikov-rynka/"}],"sourceBodySha256":"d0bdb602832d24f0790aba072f3c026c358e4bc824f142b052def8b14bac6284"}')}}]);